# Delta Specs: advanced-robustness

## circuit-breaker

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: CircuitBreaker States
The system MUST implement a CircuitBreaker with CLOSED, OPEN, HALF_OPEN states. CLOSED passes calls normally and counts failures. OPEN fails calls immediately. HALF_OPEN allows a single probe call.

- CLOSED→OPEN: failures reach threshold (default 5) → transitions to OPEN
- OPEN→HALF_OPEN: recovery timeout elapses (default 30s) → transitions to HALF_OPEN
- HALF_OPEN→CLOSED: probe succeeds → transitions to CLOSED; counter resets
- HALF_OPEN→OPEN: probe fails → transitions back to OPEN

### Requirement: Async Support
The circuit breaker MUST support async wrapping via `await breaker.call(coro)`.

## retry-policy

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: RetryPolicy Configuration
The system MUST provide RetryPolicy with max_retries (default 3), base_delay (default 1s), max_delay (default 60s), jitter (default True).

### Requirement: Exponential Backoff
The system MUST apply exponential backoff: delay = min(base_delay * 2^attempt, max_delay).

### Requirement: Async Retry
The system MUST support `await retry_policy.retry(coro)` for async coroutines.

## resilient-notifier

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: ResilientNotifier Wrapper
The system MUST provide ResilientNotifier wrapping any Notifier, applying RetryPolicy to each send() call.

### Requirement: Bounded Queue
The system MUST queue failed notifications into a bounded in-memory queue (default 1000). Oldest entries evicted when full.

### Requirement: Persistent Queue
The system SHALL persist queued notifications to a local JSONL file surviving process restarts.

### Requirement: Flush Mechanism
The system MUST provide flush() that retries all queued notifications.

## knowledge-store-health

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: KnowledgeStoreHealthCheck
The system MUST provide KnowledgeStoreHealthCheck with async check() that writes a probe record, reads it back, and returns HealthStatus.

### Requirement: Health Status TTL
The system SHALL cache health status with configurable TTL (default 60s).

### Requirement: Probe Record Cleanup
The system MUST clean up probe records after a successful check.

## llm-circuit-breaker

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: LLM Circuit Breaker Integration
The system MUST wrap LLM API calls with a CircuitBreaker before the existing fallback chain in LLMResearchAgent. When OPEN, the LLM call is skipped and fallback to classic ResearchAgent occurs immediately.

### Requirement: Fallback Chain Preservation
The existing fallback chain (LLM → classic ResearchAgent) MUST be preserved. The circuit breaker is an additional guard.

## llm-research

### MODIFIED Requirements

### Requirement: Error Handling — Fallback
If the LLM call fails, the system MUST fall back to classic ResearchAgent. The LLM call MUST be wrapped by a CircuitBreaker. When OPEN, the LLM call is skipped and fallback occurs immediately.
(Previously: LLM call attempted regardless of circuit state)

### Requirement: Rate Limiting & Caching
The system MUST reuse TokenBucket for rate limiting and SqliteCache for response caching. The circuit breaker failure counter is incremented on rate-limit errors.

## knowledge-storage

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: KnowledgeStore Health Check
The system MUST expose health_check() on KnowledgeStore returning HealthStatus by writing and reading a probe record.

### Requirement: Write Buffering When Circuit Open
The system MUST buffer writes when the circuit breaker is OPEN. Buffered writes are replayed when the circuit transitions to CLOSED. Buffer is bounded (default 1000 entries); oldest evicted when full.

### MODIFIED Requirements

### Requirement: Metadata Indexing
The system MUST maintain a metadata index (knowledge/index.yaml). The system MUST also expose health_check() as defined in the ADDED requirements.
(Previously: index.yaml only; no health reporting capability)

## autonomous-monitor

### ADDED Requirements

### Requirement: Monitor Integrates KnowledgeStore Health
The daemon MUST check store health at each compute interval and include status in heartbeat and metrics output. Unhealthy store triggers STORE_UNHEALTHY WARNING alert.

### MODIFIED Requirements

### Requirement: Alert Dispatch
The daemon MUST route alerts via NotifierDispatcher. The system MAY include store_health in the details field when store health is degraded.
(Previously: alerts did not include KnowledgeStore health status)

### Requirement: Time-Series Persistence
The daemon SHALL persist metrics and alerts to Knowledge Lake. The system SHALL also persist store health status entries with metric_name "store_health".
(Previously: only metrics and alerts persisted; store health not in time-series)
